# Project: Moodle Digital Twin

## Stack
- Backend: FastAPI + SQLAlchemy, async routes
- DB: PostgreSQL (or SQLite for local dev)
- Moodle access: Web Services REST API only — no direct DB access unless explicitly told otherwise
- ML: XGBoost, scikit-learn
- Frontend: Streamlit
- LLM layer: Groq API

## Conventions
- All Moodle API responses validated through Pydantic schemas before use
- Never assume a Moodle Web Service function exists from memory — verify against the enabled-function list I provide
- No raw SQL outside a dedicated data-access layer
- Time-respecting train/test splits only — never randomly shuffle time-series student data
- Write-back/messaging logic must live in an isolated `sandbox/` module, never in the main pipeline

## Current phase
Local Moodle instance via Docker. Real university access not yet granted. All work targets local instance, config swappable to production via env vars only.
